{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "John Meets Sandra", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "How Would You Rate It?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.   Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.   Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.   Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Agreeing and Disagreeing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use different phrases to agree and disagree tactfully (politely).<br/> Generally, you use the Present Simple Tense in the negative to disagree.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "At the workplace or when working in a group, we ask for others' opinion with questions such as:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>What do you think?</li> <li>I'm interested in your feedback/input.</li> <li>Please let me know your thoughts.</li> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We show agreement or disagreement with statements in the chart below.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Agreeing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Disagreeing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I agree with you 100 percent.</br> I couldn't agree with you more.</br> That's so true.</br> You're absolutely right.</br> Absolutely.</br> That's exactly how I feel.</br> For sure ...</br> You have a point there.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I don't think so.</br> I doubt it.</br> I'm afraid I disagree.</br> I beg to differ.</br> Not exactly.</br> That's not always true.</br> I'm not sure if ...</br> I see what you're saying, but ...</br> I don't know about that ...<br/>It might be problematic.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Comparatives & Superlatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use adjectives to compare two things. These are called <span class=\"strong\">comparative</span> adjectives. You can also use adjectives to compare one item with the rest of a group. These are called <span class=\"strong\">superlative</span> adjectives.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Selling good quality products is <span class=\"underline\">as</span> important <span class=\"underline\">as</span> good customer service.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are <span class=\"underline\">more</span> people at this workshop <span class=\"underline\">than</span> the last one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There was <span class=\"underline\">less</span> time allotted for the last workshop <span class=\"underline\">than</span> this one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For comparative adjectives, you can use the structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul> <li><span class=\"strong\">as</span> + adjective + <span class=\"strong\">as</span></li> <li>adjective (<span class=\"strong\">-er</span>) <span class=\"strong\">than</span></li> <li><span class=\"strong\">more/less</span> + adjective + <span class=\"strong\">than</span></li></ul>  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Adjectives with 3 syllables or more use <span class=\"strong\">more/less</span> + adjective + <span class=\"strong\">than</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For superlative adjectives, you can use:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>adjective (<span class=\"strong\">-est</span>)</li> <li><span class=\"strong\">most/least</span> + adjective</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Adjectives with 3 syllables or more use <span class=\"strong italic\">most/least</span> + <span class=\"italic\">adjective</span>.</br> The adjectives <span class=\"italic\">good</span> and <span class=\"italic\">bad</span> are irregular adjectives. They do not follow the same rules.", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "enriching", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very good quality or useful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: John attended a very enriching workshop last week. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "problematic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "describes a situation that's a problem", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To not have a computer for a presentation is problematic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "occupied", "type": "name"}, {"content": "busy doing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All of the guides are occupied with tours this week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to proceed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to begin or to continue", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The manager likes my ideas, so he will proceed with my plan.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "no doubt about it", "type": "name"}, {"content": "so sure about something that there is no doubt", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I know she would do a very good job. There's no doubt about it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to put it on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to organize and hold an event", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Many people came to the workshop last week so the manager asked me to put it on again.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "compulsory", "type": "name"}, {"content": "required by a rule or law", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is compulsory for everyone working on the ship to have safety training.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Ask your partner which shop in your city has the best customer service. Choose one kind of shop to talk about, i.e. computer stores or supermarkets.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask your partner to tell you 3 reasons why their service is better. Compare them to the other stores in the same category.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare your reasons with your partner's. Express your agreement or disagreement in English. <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/><br/> <br/> <br/>", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I identify what makes good customer service.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write sentences to compare two things.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for another person's opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express agreement and disagreement in English.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn5le07ob10re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le07ob10re2img05.jpg", "time": "10", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-100\">Mr. Micklewhite</span>: Hello, John. Thanks for coming in. I appreciated your feedback on the workshop. Tell me more about it.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: In my opinion, it was certainly the most enriching workshop up to now. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Micklewhite</span>: No doubt about it. Would you say that customer service is a better topic than others?"}, {"image": "engenn5le07ob10re2img02.jpg", "time": "17000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-100\">John</span>: Absolutely. The focus of our service is on passengers. So, it's the most important.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Micklewhite</span>: You have a point there. I'll inquire with U.S. Tours to put it on for every employee.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: The way I see it, it might be problematic making it compulsory for every guide."}, {"image": "engenn5le07ob10re2img05.jpg", "time": "34000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-100\">Mr. Micklewhite</span>: What makes you say that?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Well, they're all occupied with tours and planning. However, if we hold it earlier in the morning than before, it might work.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Micklewhite</span>: Good thinking, John. Let's proceed with that plan."}], "audiosrc": "engenn5le07ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le07ob10re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can agree and disagree tactfully.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk or report about actions, events or people.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can make comparisons. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What is the most interesting thing you learned at work or at school?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Can you suggest a topic you would like to learn about?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let me know what you think!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}]}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " Mr. Micklewhite wants to know John's opinion. What does John suggest?", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1]}, {"template_override